SDUSD::principalOf
├── when shares are minted through deposit or mint
│   ├── it should record the actual DUSD paid against the receiver
│   ├── it should exempt only the exact initial seed deposited to address(1)
│   ├── it should count ordinary first deposits and permit their full redemption
│   └── it should count later deposits to the permanent lock
├── when rewards accrue
│   └── it should leave every holder principal and total cap usage unchanged
├── when shares are transferred or transferred via allowance
│   ├── it should carry the sender proportional principal to the recipient
│   ├── it should merge that basis with any existing recipient basis
│   ├── it should preserve total principal and cap usage
│   ├── it should preserve principal on self-transfers and zero transfers
│   ├── it should preserve state and the ERC20 error on a failed transfer
│   └── it should retain principal transferred to address(1) in cap usage
├── when shares are burned through withdraw or redeem
│   ├── it should remove the owner basis even when a different caller or receiver is used
│   ├── it should leave rounding remainders with the owner until their full exit
│   ├── it should use that holder average basis for partial exits from mixed deposits
│   └── it should remove all remaining owner principal on a full exit
├── when a new holder repeatedly deposits and redeems after rewards
│   ├── it should restore the full deposit headroom after every complete round trip
│   └── it should leave existing holders principal unchanged
├── when several beneficial holders share a custodial address
│   └── it should document that custody round trips can blend and reassign their principal bases
└── when deposits, rewards, transfers and redemptions are interleaved
    ├── it should conserve the sum of holder principal as depositCapUsage
    ├── it should leave no principal attached to a zero share balance
    └── it should clear all non-seed principal after every holder exits
